            <ArticleTitle>Catalytic stereospecific O-glycosylation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2040-2043</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc10076g</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new simple protocol, using TMSNTf2 or Tf2NH as the catalyst, for the activation of trichloroacetimidate donors is described. This O-glycosylation proceeds with stereospecific inversion of the donor configuration. The scope of the protocol has been investigated using common glycosyl donors reacting with simple alcohols as well as sugar acceptors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
